-- title:
--   Dual-number points of the deformation ring separated by (u,v)
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and write $\mathbb{Z}_{q^2} =$ `Zp2 q` for the Witt vectors of $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$. Let $O^{nr}$ be a characteristic-zero discrete valuation domain which is a $\mathbb{Z}_q$-algebra, adically complete for the ideal generated by the image of $q$, that ideal being maximal, with algebraically closed residue field $k$; let $\iota : \mathbb{Z}_{q^2} \to O^{nr}$ be a ring map and $X_0$ a formal $O_D$-module of dimension $2$ over $k$ for $j_0 = \bar{\cdot}\circ\iota$ (a commutative two-variable formal group law with $\mathbb{Z}_{q^2}$-action and uniformiser series $\varpi$ satisfying $\varpi\circ\varpi = [q]$ and $\varpi\circ[a] = [\mathrm{Frob}\,a]\circ\varpi$) which is special, in the sense that $\mathrm{Lie}$ is the direct sum of the complementary invertible submodules `lieZero` and `lieOne`, and of height $4$. Let $R$ be a Noetherian local $O^{nr}$-algebra, complete for its maximal ideal, with $\mathrm{res}_R : R \to k$ lifting the residue map of $O^{nr}$, and $\mathcal{X}$ a formal $O_D$-module over $R$ together with an isomorphism $w_u : \mathcal{X}\otimes_R k \to X_0$. Assume the pro-representability hypothesis $(R,\mathcal{X},w_u)$: for every local Artinian $O^{nr}$-algebra $A$ with surjective $\mathrm{res}_A : A \to k$ compatible with the residue map, every formal $O_D$-module $X$ over $A$ that is special for $(\mathrm{algebraMap}\circ\iota)$ and of height $4$, and every isomorphism $w : X\otimes_A k \to X_0$, there is a unique $O^{nr}$-algebra map $\chi : R \to A$ with $\mathrm{res}_A\circ\chi = \mathrm{res}_R$ admitting an isomorphism $v : \mathcal{X}\otimes_R A \to X$ with $v$ reduced and followed by $w$ having the same series as $w_u$. Assume further the double-point condition that the linear part of $\varpi_{X_0}$ annihilates both `lieZero` and `lieOne` of $X_0$; let $e_0 \in \mathrm{lieZero}(\mathcal{X})$, $e_1 \in \mathrm{lieOne}(\mathcal{X})$ form an $R$-basis of $\mathrm{Lie}\,\mathcal{X} = R^2$ (every element is uniquely $c_0 e_0 + c_1 e_1$), and let $u, v \in R$ satisfy $\lambda(\varpi_{\mathcal{X}})e_0 = u\,e_1$ and $\lambda(\varpi_{\mathcal{X}})e_1 = v\,e_0$, where $\lambda$ denotes the matrix of linear coefficients. Then any two ring homomorphisms $\chi, \chi' : R \to k[\varepsilon]$ whose composites with the projection $k[\varepsilon]\to k$ equal $\mathrm{res}_R$ and whose restrictions to $O^{nr}$ are the residue map followed by $k \to k[\varepsilon]$, and which agree at $u$ and at $v$, are equal.
--
--   This is the injectivity of the tangent map on first-order deformations of a special formal $O_D$-module at a double point: a deformation over the dual numbers is pinned down by the two Lie coordinates of the uniformiser in the basis adapted to the eigenline decomposition. It is used in the Čerednik–Drinfeld part of the argument to identify the maximal ideal of the deformation ring with the ideal generated by $u$, $v$ and the image of the maximal ideal of $O^{nr}$, and in the recognition of rigidified formal modules through their dual-number reductions.
